WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.040
It's got the largest cast, and cash prize, in&nbsp;
TV history, but is "Squid Game: The Challenge"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.080
even legit? Here's why some contestants&nbsp;
say the game was rigged from the start.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.160
Anyone who watched Netflix's hit 2021&nbsp;
South Korean drama "Squid Game" knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.280
that the fictional dystopian game in question —&nbsp;
wherein 456 people desperate for financial help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.440
fight to the death for a $4.56 million&nbsp;
cash prize — is brutal and unforgiving.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.640
According to a report in Rolling&nbsp;
Stone from February 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.680
the streamer's reality competition&nbsp;
show based on the series — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:40.120
offering the same cash prize — was,&nbsp;
if not lethal, also pretty brutal.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.840
Not only were filming conditions during&nbsp;
one specific game reportedly horrible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.400
but some former contestants made claims&nbsp;
that the entire thing was rigged.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.600
For their part, Netflix and its&nbsp;
co-producing studio partners deny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.480
claims of a fixed game, telling Rolling Stone,

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.640
"Any suggestion that the competition is rigged&nbsp;
or claims of serious harm to players are simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.020
untrue. We’ve taken all the appropriate safety&nbsp;
precautions, including after care for contestants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:07.120
— and an independent adjudicator is overseeing&nbsp;
each game to ensure it’s fair to everyone."

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.200
But some contestants were exceedingly blunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.360
about what went down when they&nbsp;
spoke to the outlet. One said,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.120
"It was just the cruelest, meanest thing I've&nbsp;
ever been through. We were a human horse race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.320
and they were treating us like horses out in&nbsp;
the cold, racing, and [the race] was fixed."

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.440
So, how was the race fixed, exactly? One&nbsp;
part of the exposé claimed that during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.480
the filming of the "Red Light, Green Light" game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.280
some contestants successfully crossed the&nbsp;
finish line, only to still get eliminated.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.960
Their ink-filled "squib packs" — which simulate&nbsp;
gunshots and signal a contestant's elimination —&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.000
allegedly exploded way after the fact. That group&nbsp;
didn't take it well. One contestant recalled,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.960
"It really wasn't a game show. It was a TV show,&nbsp;
and we were basically extras in a TV show."

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.720
We all know that reality shows&nbsp;
manipulate scenarios and make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.080
careful edits to ensure certain outcomes.&nbsp;
Contestants on "The Challenge," though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.240
have alleged that the on-set behavior from&nbsp;
producers was nothing short of egregious.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.200
Take this example from a contestant who claims&nbsp;
that she was eliminated even though she got across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.920
the "Red Light, Green Light" finish line with&nbsp;
five seconds still on the clock. It was then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.600
as she was waiting to leave, that&nbsp;
she saw that a contestant and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.920
mother were still being filmed ... and&nbsp;
not only that, but the show allegedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.440
added time to the clock off-camera just to&nbsp;
feature the duo. The contestant claimed,

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.520
"This kid is sitting at the&nbsp;
finish line, he's crying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:20.200
and cameras are on him and he's waiting for&nbsp;
his mom. They added [more time] to the clock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.880
for her to get across because she was one of&nbsp;
the people that they wanted to be in the show."

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.920
"My mom, she was like a superstar&nbsp;
athlete. It's like, I just feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:32.880
like she's going to—she's going to outlast me&nbsp;
and embarrass me in front of all my family."

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.080
Regarding the nine-hour shoot for the "Red&nbsp;
Light, Green Light" game, which was filmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.200
inside an airplane hangar, contestants&nbsp;
made some extremely serious accusations.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.600
Namely, they said that they were forced to&nbsp;
maintain frozen poses for the bulk of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.600
nine hours, only moving from time to time ...&nbsp;
a condition made worse by the fact that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.680
weren't appropriately dressed for the allegedly&nbsp;
freezing cold temperatures inside the hangar.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.400
The icy conditions — as low as 14 Fahrenheit,&nbsp;
according to the Rolling Stone report — led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.840
to some contestants getting sick and collapsing,&nbsp;
and while medics attended to the fallen players,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.400
people in pink "Squid Game" guard suits&nbsp;
would block the process from view so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.920
everybody else could stay frozen&nbsp;
in place. One contestant revealed,

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.400
"People were beating themselves up, including&nbsp;
myself, around the fact that you've got a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:15.400
girl convulsing and we're all stood there&nbsp;
like statues. On what planet is that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.480
humane? [...] It played on our morals&nbsp;
and it's sick. It's absolutely sick."

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:23.200
Other injuries contestants say they incurred&nbsp;
during filming include a herniated disc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.040
a torn knee tendon, pneumonia, and ear infections.&nbsp;
One contestant told Rolling Stone that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.520
despite the game's origins, a brutal survival&nbsp;
experience wasn't what they were expecting:

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.600
"It's not like we signed up for 'Naked&nbsp;
and Afraid' or 'Survivor,' where you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.960
gonna eat ants and it's gonna be&nbsp;
grim — that was not the game."

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.560
And another contestant mused,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.640
"The funny thing is, equality and fairness was&nbsp;
the main theme of the original Squid Game."

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.360
Was it, though? The competition&nbsp;
depicted in "Squid Game" was a brutal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.160
predatory exercise created by wealthy&nbsp;
sadists who treated human life with little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.960
to no respect. The contestants were, to put&nbsp;
it lightly, manipulated into participating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.960
and were targeted due to their&nbsp;
precarious financial positions.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:04.280
Not only that, but if they moved during "Red&nbsp;
Light, Green Light," or lost a game of tug of war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:09.240
they were quite literally killed on the spot. None&nbsp;
of this is to say that the alleged misconduct on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.160
the set of "Squid Game: The Challenge" is&nbsp;
acceptable in the slightest. It is to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.800
though, that perhaps a reality&nbsp;
competition series based on such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:20.160
a terrifying and ugly prospect is sort&nbsp;
of an iffy concept in the first place.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.520
As another contestant put it,

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:26.200
"There's $4.5 million up for grabs [...] These&nbsp;
people were willing to die. [Someone] says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.040
'I'm going home with this, I don't care what&nbsp;
it takes.' I think the producers wanted that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.445
They wanted people to not think about their&nbsp;
health, to not care about their safety."

